  "id": "organizational-justice",
  "term": "organizational justice",
  "definition": "Organizational justice is the degree of fairness employees perceive in how they are treated within an organization. Lower organizational justice means feeling less fairly treated at work and is linked in this source to greater ambivalence toward the organization and higher work-related stress.",
